-- MRCP Part 2 Clinical Pharmacology and Therapeutics -- batch 1 (50 questions)
-- Sub-topics: Adverse drug reactions, Anticoagulation & antiplatelet therapy, Drug interactions,
-- Pharmacokinetics, Poisoning & overdose, Prescribing in renal & hepatic impairment

  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 68-year-old man with persistent atrial fibrillation has been taking amiodarone 200 mg once daily for 14 months. He now reports progressive exertional dyspnoea and a dry cough over 6 weeks. Examination reveals fine bibasal crackles and oxygen saturation of 91% on air. High-resolution CT chest shows bilateral ground-glass opacification with subpleural fibrotic change. Echocardiogram is unchanged from baseline and there is no evidence of heart failure.',
  'What is the most appropriate next step in management?',
  array['amiodarone pulmonary toxicity','drug-induced lung disease','ADR']
),
