  'draft', 'advanced',
  'A 58-year-old man with gout is started on allopurinol 100 mg daily after a second attack. Three weeks later he develops fever, a widespread morbilliform rash affecting over 60% of body surface area, facial oedema and cervical lymphadenopathy. Blood tests show eosinophilia (2.8 x10^9/L), ALT 310 U/L and creatinine 145 micromol/L (baseline 80). He has not been tested for HLA-B*58:01 prior to starting treatment.',
  'What is the most appropriate immediate management?',
  array['DRESS syndrome','allopurinol hypersensitivity','severe cutaneous adverse reaction']
),
